WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.506
The pair source passes a Bell check on a
separate batch of simulated pairs.

00:00:04.506 --> 00:00:07.972
The receiver also delivers zero and one
perfectly.

00:00:07.972 --> 00:00:10.953
A user says their qubit changes on
delivery.

00:00:10.953 --> 00:00:13.226
Could all three checks still be right?

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.981
Alice and Bob share a fresh pair.

00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:20.267
Alice has a third qubit to send.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:24.584
You control its preparation and how the
tester reads Bob's output.

00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:28.807
Would you repeat the zero test, or send
plus and check for plus?

00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:30.121
Pause and choose.

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:35.264
Send plus.

00:00:35.264 --> 00:00:39.907
A healthy receiver returns plus every
time when checked in the matching basis.

00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:42.926
This receiver returns plus only half the
time.

00:00:42.926 --> 00:00:44.221
Open the trace.

00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:47.845
There are four equally likely messages
Alice can send Bob.

00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:50.760
Follow message one zero.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.946
Its first bit tells Bob to correct the
phase.

00:00:53.946 --> 00:00:56.495
Its second bit asks for no flip.

00:00:56.495 --> 00:00:57.954
Both bits arrive.

00:00:57.954 --> 00:01:00.319
The broken receiver applies no gate.

00:01:00.319 --> 00:01:05.117
The tester expects plus and reads minus
on every delivery with this message.

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:08.666
Here's what the zero and one tests
missed.

00:01:08.666 --> 00:01:11.568
Plus has two components with the same
sign.

00:01:11.568 --> 00:01:14.815
Minus has the same sizes but opposite
signs.

00:01:14.815 --> 00:01:17.959
A zero or one measurement sees only the
sizes.

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:22.020
Measuring in the plus and minus basis
detects the sign difference.

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:25.124
Give the first bit its job back.

00:01:25.124 --> 00:01:30.129
When it is one, Bob applies Z, which
changes the sign of the one component.

00:01:30.129 --> 00:01:32.520
Replay the same message and input.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.263
This time the output passes the plus
check.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.715
Run all six inputs.

00:01:37.715 --> 00:01:40.291
The first two never exposed the bug.

00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:43.603
The other four move from half to all
deliveries passing.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:47.586
Keep a test with both the plus input and
the one zero message.

00:01:47.586 --> 00:01:52.235
If the phase correction disappears again,
that test fails every time.
